    routePath: 'bismarck',
    LLM: 'Game: Bismarck. 3 players. 52 cards. 16 tricks per deal. 12 deals total. 4 contracts (Sang, Pass, Spader, Valfri) â€” each used once per player. Forehand picks up 4 face-up cards, discards 4, chooses contract. Quotas: forehand 8 (or 4 in Pass), others 4 (or 6 in Pass). Score: +1/-1 per trick over/under quota. Zero-sum.',
    Player: "You're forehand. The 4 face-up cards are: Aâ™  Kâ™  7â™¥ 3â™¦. Your 16 dealt cards include Qâ™  Jâ™  10â™  and scattered mid-range cards. You haven't played Spader yet. Do you take the spade powerhouse and declare Spader, or save it and go for Sang with your strong high cards?",
    tagline: 'Choose your contract. Meet your quota. Outscore the other two.',
