      timeline: [
        "1941: Battleship Bismarck sunk â€” likely inspiration for the game's name.",
        '1944: First known published rules of the card game appear in Sweden.',
        'Late 20th century: Spreads to Britain, Finland, Portugal, and Estonia.',
        'Present: Played in multiple variants across Northern and Western Europe.',
      ],
      evolution: "Bismarck belongs to the 'quota whist' family where players score based on deviation from a target number of tricks. It shares DNA with Mizerka (Poland) and other European three-player trick-taking games. The compulsory contract rotation system ensures variety across a full game.",
      cultural: 'A distinctively Scandinavian card game that reflects the Northern European love of structured trick-taking games with strategic depth.',
