        rules: {
          objective: 'Over 12 deals (each player is forehand 4 times), score the highest cumulative total by managing your tricks relative to your quota.',
          gameplay: 'Forehand leads to the first trick. Any card may be led. Players must follow suit if possible; if void, may play any card. With trumps the trick is won by the highest trump; with no trumps, by the highest card of the led suit. There is no obligation to beat or to overtrump. The winner of each trick leads to the next. After 16 tricks, players are scored against their quota for the chosen contract.',
          keyRules: [
            'Forehand sees 4 face-up cards BEFORE choosing their contract â€” critical information for decision-making.',
            'Forehand picks up the 4 face-up cards and discards 4, keeping 16 for play.',
            'Each contract must be used exactly once per player over 12 deals.',
            '16 tricks per deal (3 players Ã— 16 cards Ã· 3? No â€” 48 cards Ã· 3 = 16 each, so 16 tricks).',
            'Zero-sum scoring: all three scores always add to zero.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'As forehand, evaluate the 4 face-up cards carefully before choosing your contract. With many high cards and a strong suit, choose Sang or a trump contract. With weak cards, choose Pass.',
          intermediate: "Contract sequencing: save your most flexible contract (Valfri) for last so you can adapt to your hand. Spader should be chosen when you naturally have good spades. Don't waste Valfri on spades if you haven't played Spader yet.",
          advanced: 'In Sang (no-trump, win tricks), count the cards: with 16 tricks, forehand needs 8 â€” exactly half. Lead your strong suits first to establish winners. In Pass (avoid tricks), avoid leading and duck with low cards. Discard strategy: when picking up the 4 face-up cards, discard to strengthen your chosen contract â€” void a suit for trump contracts, or shed high cards for Pass.',
          tips: [
            'The 4 face-up cards give forehand a 20-card hand â€” use the discard to tailor your hand perfectly.',
            "Track the 4 discarded cards â€” they're out of play and affect trick counting.",
            'In Pass, the quota is only 4 for forehand â€” try to take exactly 4 or fewer.',
            'Contract sequencing over 12 deals is a meta-strategy: plan which contracts to play early vs. late.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
