          deckDescription: 'One standard international 52-card deck without jokers, used in a three-player Swedish quota whist game where contracts and trick quotas, not bidding, drive scoring and play.',
          suitDescription: 'Four French suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs). In Spader and Valfri contracts one suit is trump; in Sang and Pass there is no trump suit, but players must follow the led suit.',
          rankDescription: 'Thirteen ranks per suit, ace high down to two, as in standard whist. Trick winners are determined by highest trump when trumps apply, otherwise by highest card of the led suit.',
